<div class="catalogue-body">
  <section class="catalogue-intro flush">
    <h2>Capability before configuration.</h2><p>
      A blueprint supplies the questions, workflows and rules an owner should not have to imagine from scratch. Its applicability must be confirmed with the business.
    </p>
  </section><section class="catalogue-panel">
    <div class="wb-actions">
      <h2>{@blueprint["name"]}</h2><Workbench.status
        label="Demonstrated · not installed"
        tone="warning"
      />
    </div><p>{@blueprint["outcome"]}</p><p>Blueprint version {@blueprint["version"]}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="catalogue-panel catalogue-space">
    <h2>Domain concepts, behaviour and compositions</h2><p>
      This blueprint packages business definitions and presentation bindings together. Bindings connect projections to controls and inputs to named commands.
    </p>
    <div class="wb-actions catalogue-space">
      <.link
        :for={id <- Enum.map(@blueprint["domain_model"]["nodes"], & &1["id"])}
        patch={"/dev/catalogue/domain?node=#{id}"}
        class="catalogue-relation"
      >{Business.Catalogue.Domain.get(id)["name"]}</.link>
    </div>
    <.link
      patch={"/dev/catalogue/model?node=#{Enum.find(@blueprint["design_model"]["nodes"], &(&1["kind"] == "Blueprint"))["id"]}"}
      class="wb-button secondary"
    >Explore the design model</.link>
    <div class="wb-actions catalogue-space">
      <.link
        :for={id <- @blueprint["compositions"]}
        patch={"/dev/catalogue/graph?node=#{id}"}
        class="catalogue-relation"
      >{Business.Catalogue.Components.get(id).title}</.link>
    </div>
    <.bindings bindings={@blueprint["presentation_bindings"]} />
  </section><div class="catalogue-grid flush catalogue-space">
    <section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Ask the owner</h2><ol>
        <li :for={question <- @blueprint["questions"]}>{question}</li>
      </ol>
    </section><section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Business rules</h2><ul>
        <li :for={rule <- @blueprint["rules"]}>{rule}</li>
      </ul>
    </section><section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Acceptance scenarios</h2><ul>
        <li :for={example <- @blueprint["acceptance"] || []}>{example}</li>
      </ul><.link patch="/dev/catalogue/compositions" class="wb-button catalogue-space">Explore the working composition</.link>
    </section><section class="catalogue-panel">
      <h2>Boundaries & dependencies</h2><p>
        Each blueprint declares its domain and authority boundaries. Validate these against the customer’s business before implementation.
      </p><h3 class="catalogue-space">Not yet implemented</h3><ul>
        <li :for={gap <- @blueprint["not_implemented"] || []}>{gap}</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div><p class="catalogue-footnote">
    Source: {@blueprint["source"]} · Versioned snapshot carried by the starter; no Bedrock runtime calls.
  </p>
</div>
